---
name: funke-add-editor-panel
description: Use when adding or changing an ImGui editor panel / window in Funke-Editor. Triggers on "add an editor panel", "new panel", "editor window", "tool window", "Tools menu", "command palette entry", "ImGuiEditorLayer", "OnAttach / OnDetach / OnPreRender", "m_Show…", "EditorUI", "SetNextWindowAsNativeDialog", "NextWindowDefaultSize", "EmptyState", "ProfilerPanel / PackageManagerPanel / BuildProfilesPanel / EditorPreferencesPanel / SpriteEditorPanel", "worker thread in a panel", "panel freezes the editor", or work in `Funke-Editor/src/Gui/*Panel.{hpp,cpp}` and `Funke-Editor/src/Systems/ImGuiEditorLayer*.{hpp,cpp}`. Covers the panel class shape (Initialize / Render(bool* pOpen) / Shutdown), window setup conventions, the ImGuiEditorLayer integration sites (member + flag, OnAttach, OnDetach, the render call in OnPreRender, menu + command palette), lazy-init panels, and the async worker pattern (shared_ptr state + mutex + atomic + std::thread + main-thread poll).
---

# Add an Editor Panel

Editor panels are plain classes in `Funke-Editor/src/Gui/`, owned by value in `ImGuiEditorLayer` and drawn from its `OnPreRender`. Reference panels:

| Panel | Shape worth copying |
|---|---|
| `Gui/ProfilerPanel.{hpp,cpp}` | Pure view over engine state; `Initialize/Render(bool*)/Shutdown`; compiled stub when `FUNKE_PROFILER_ENABLED` is off |
| `Gui/BuildProfilesPanel.{hpp,cpp}` | Lazy-initialized on first open; dirty-flag rescans; status strip; deferred popup opens |
| `Gui/EditorPreferencesPanel.{hpp,cpp}` | First-frame-open hook (`m_WasOpenLastFrame`); deferred modal opens (`m_OpenSaveLayoutRequest`/`m_OpenDeleteLayoutRequest`); search-filtered sections (`PreferenceSectionVisible`) |
| `Gui/SpriteEditorPanel.{hpp,cpp}` | Opened with data (`OpenTexture`), result handed back (`TakeSlicesApplied()`) |
| `Gui/PackageManagerPanel.{hpp,cpp}` | Async workers; `Render()` without `pOpen` — the layer wraps `Begin/End` |

Some windows (Log, Build, Project Settings, Project/Asset browser) are **not** classes — they're `ImGuiEditorLayer::Render…Panel()` methods in `Systems/ImGuiEditorLayerPanels.cpp`. Prefer a class in `Gui/` for anything new and non-trivial; `ImGuiEditorLayerPanels.cpp` is already ~4.6k lines.

## Class skeleton

`Funke-Editor/src/Gui/MyPanel.hpp`:

```cpp
#pragma once

#include <string>
#include <vector>

namespace Funke {

	class MyPanel {
	public:
		void Initialize();          // one-time setup; no ImGui calls
		void Shutdown();            // join workers, free resources; no ImGui calls
		void Render(bool* pOpen);   // every frame; pOpen flips false on the title-bar X

	private:
		void RefreshIfDirty();
		void RenderToolbar();
		void RenderList();

		std::vector<std::string> m_Items;
		bool m_Dirty = true;
		char m_SearchBuffer[256]{};

		std::string m_StatusMessage;
		bool m_StatusIsError = false;
	};

} // namespace Funke
```

`Funke-Editor/src/Gui/MyPanel.cpp`:

```cpp
#include "Gui/MyPanel.hpp"

#include "Gui/EditorUI.hpp"
#include "Gui/ImGuiImplWebGPU.hpp"
#include "Project/ProjectManager.hpp"

namespace Funke {

	void MyPanel::Render(bool* pOpen) {
		if (!pOpen || !*pOpen) return;

		ImGuiImplWebGPU::SetNextWindowAsNativeDialog();   // floating tool window in its own OS window
		EditorUI::NextWindowDefaultSize();
		if (!ImGui::Begin("My Panel", pOpen)) {
			ImGui::End();
			return;
		}

		if (!ProjectManager::GetCurrentProject()) {
			EditorUI::EmptyState("No project open.", "Open a project to use this panel.");
			ImGui::End();
			return;
		}

		RefreshIfDirty();
		RenderToolbar();
		RenderList();
		ImGui::End();
	}

} // namespace Funke
```

Conventions:
- **PCH:** `Funke-Editor/premake5.lua` force-includes `EditorPch.hpp` (ImGui, Vec2, Scene/entt are already in it). Include your own header first; don't add churny headers to `EditorPch.hpp` (rule in its header comment).
- **Look:** compose from `Gui/EditorUI.hpp` (`Button(label, ButtonVariant)`, `SearchField`, `BeginToolbar/EndToolbar`, `BeginCard/EndCard`, `Badge`, `EmptyState`, `StatusText(Tone, …)`, `DialogFooter`, `Tooltip`) and `Gui/ImGuiUtils.hpp` (`ToggleSwitch`, `Switch`, …). Colours come from `EditorTheme` — never hardcode them in a panel.
- **Native dialog:** `ImGuiImplWebGPU::SetNextWindowAsNativeDialog()` (`Funke-Engine/src/Gui/ImGuiImplWebGPU.hpp`) sets the next window's class. Call it before the matching `Begin`/`BeginPopupModal`, with no intervening window begin; other setup such as `EditorUI::NextWindowDefaultSize()` may follow it. Used by Profiler, Build Profiles, Preferences, Package Manager. Dockable views (Sprite Editor, Log) skip it.
- **Always pair `Begin` with `End`**, including the early-return path where `Begin` returned false.
- Per-frame cost: cache + dirty flag (`m_Dirty`, `m_ManifestsDirty` in `PackageManagerPanel`) instead of scanning disk each frame. Instrument with the profiler if a panel drops frames (`funke-add-profiler`).

## Integration sites in ImGuiEditorLayer

### 1 — Member + visibility flag
`Funke-Editor/src/Systems/ImGuiEditorLayer.hpp`: add `#include "Gui/MyPanel.hpp"` next to the other `Gui/*Panel.hpp` includes, and in the private section (near `m_ShowProfiler` / `m_ProfilerPanel`):

```cpp
bool    m_ShowMyPanel = false;
MyPanel m_MyPanel;
```

### 2 — Initialize: `ImGuiEditorLayer::OnAttach` (`ImGuiEditorLayer.cpp`)
Next to `m_ProfilerPanel.Initialize(); m_SpriteEditorPanel.Initialize();`:
```cpp
m_MyPanel.Initialize();
```
**Or lazy-init** on first show when setup is expensive or needs a project — the `RenderBuildProfilesPanel` pattern (`ImGuiEditorLayerPanels.cpp`):
```cpp
void ImGuiEditorLayer::RenderMyPanel() {
	if (!m_ShowMyPanel) return;
	if (!m_MyPanelInitialized) { m_MyPanel.Initialize(); m_MyPanelInitialized = true; }
	m_MyPanel.Render(&m_ShowMyPanel);
}
```

### 3 — Shutdown: `ImGuiEditorLayer::OnDetach` (`ImGuiEditorLayer.cpp`)
Next to `m_ProfilerPanel.Shutdown(); m_SpriteEditorPanel.Shutdown(); m_EditorPreferencesPanel.Shutdown();` (these run after the layer's own build/reserialize workers are joined and before WebGPU teardown — a panel owning GPU textures must release them here). Panels with workers go with `m_PackageManagerPanel.Shutdown()` in the "panels → icons → FBOs" block.
```cpp
m_MyPanel.Shutdown();
```

### 4 — Render: `ImGuiEditorLayer::OnPreRender` (`ImGuiEditorLayerChrome.cpp`)
Two spots:
- **Inside** `ImGui::BeginDisabled(m_BuildState > 0 || m_ReserializeState > 0)` … `EndDisabled()` with `RenderBuildPanel(); RenderBuildProfilesPanel(); RenderPackageManagerPanel();` — use this if the panel must be greyed out while a build/reserialize runs.
- **After** `EndDisabled()` with the Profiler / Sprite Editor — always interactive:
```cpp
if (m_ShowMyPanel) {
	m_MyPanel.Render(&m_ShowMyPanel);
}
```
(Global shortcuts live here too, e.g. `ImGui::IsKeyChordPressed(ImGuiMod_Ctrl | ImGuiKey_F6)` toggles the profiler.)

### 5 — Entry points (`ImGuiEditorLayer.cpp`)
- **Main menu** — `RenderMainMenu`: menus are `Application`, `Project` (Build, Build Profiles…, Project Settings, Package Manager), `Edit` (Undo/Redo, Preferences...), `Tools` (`ImGui::MenuItem("Profiler", "Ctrl+F6", &m_ShowProfiler);`). Gate project-dependent items with `hasProject`.
- **Command palette** (Ctrl+K) — `RenderCommandPalette`: add `{ "My Panel", nullptr, hasProject, [&]() { m_ShowMyPanel = true; } },` to the `commands[]` array.

Missing site 4 is the classic bug: it compiles, the menu flips the bool, nothing appears. New `.cpp/.hpp` files under `Funke-Editor/src/` are picked up by the `src/**.cpp` glob once premake regenerates; `scripts\dev\Build.ps1 Editor` does that automatically (`funke-build-engine`).

## Async work — the long-task pattern

ImGui runs on the main thread; anything that can exceed a frame (file I/O over many files, `dotnet`/`cmake`/Python processes, network, blocking Win32 dialogs) goes to a worker. `PackageManagerPanel` has six instances of this pattern (`AutomationTaskState`, `RegistryFetchTaskState`, `CloudInstallTaskState`, `GitInstallTaskState`, `NewPackageTaskState`, `DiskInstallTaskState`):

```cpp
struct FetchTaskState {
	std::mutex Mutex;
	std::atomic<bool> Running{ false };
	bool Finished = false;
	bool Success = false;
	std::string Error;
	std::string Result;
};
std::shared_ptr<FetchTaskState> m_FetchTask;
std::thread m_FetchWorker;

void MyPanel::StartFetch() {
	if (m_FetchTask && m_FetchTask->Running.load()) return;
	if (m_FetchWorker.joinable()) m_FetchWorker.join();
	m_FetchTask = std::make_shared<FetchTaskState>();
	m_FetchTask->Running.store(true);
	auto state = m_FetchTask;                    // capture the shared_ptr, never `this`
	m_FetchWorker = std::thread([state]() {
		std::string result, error; bool ok = /* long work */ true;
		std::scoped_lock lock(state->Mutex);
		state->Result = std::move(result); state->Error = std::move(error);
		state->Success = ok; state->Finished = true;
		state->Running.store(false);
	});
}

void MyPanel::PollFetch() {                      // call at the top of Render
	if (!m_FetchTask) return;
	bool finished = false;
	{ std::scoped_lock lock(m_FetchTask->Mutex); finished = m_FetchTask->Finished; }
	if (!finished) return;
	{ std::scoped_lock lock(m_FetchTask->Mutex); m_FetchTask->Finished = false; }
	if (m_FetchWorker.joinable()) m_FetchWorker.join();
	// consume Result/Error on the main thread: touch project state, mark dirty, set status
}

void MyPanel::Shutdown() {
	if (m_FetchWorker.joinable()) m_FetchWorker.join();
}
```

Rules (from `PackageManagerPanel`):
- **Snapshot under the lock, act outside it.** Copy fields out, release, then do work.
- **Project/engine state changes happen on the main thread** in the poll (e.g. `InstallToProject` + post-install automation after a git clone), never in the worker.
- **`Shutdown` joins every `std::thread` and waits every `std::future`** before clearing state — destroying a joinable thread is `std::terminate`, and `std::async` futures block in their destructor.
- **Blocking Win32 dialogs** (`IFileOpenDialog::Show`) run on their own worker that owns a COM STA — see `HandleDiskInstall` / `DiskInstallTaskState`.
- **Progress UI** for long jobs is the shared build-progress popup owned by the chrome: expose `bool GetActiveLoadingPopup(std::string& title, std::string& stage, float& progress)` like `PackageManagerPanel` and hook it where `OnPreRender` queries `m_PackageManagerPanel.GetActiveLoadingPopup(...)`.

## Pitfalls

- **ImGui calls in `Initialize`/`Shutdown`** — run outside a frame; defer to `Render`.
- **Another window begins after `SetNextWindowAsNativeDialog`** — that window consumes the pending class; keep the call with its intended `Begin`/`BeginPopupModal` setup.
- **Window title collisions** — the ImGui title is the ID and the `imgui.ini` key; keep it unique and stable (rename = users lose saved docking for it). Use `"Title##id"` to disambiguate.
- **Worker captures `this`** — races panel destruction. Capture the `shared_ptr` state.
- **Forgetting `Shutdown`** in `OnDetach` — hang or `std::terminate` on editor close.
- **Opening a popup from inside another ID scope** — set a request flag (`m_OpenRenamePopup`, `m_OpenDeletePopup`) and call `OpenPopup` where the `BeginPopupModal` lives (BuildProfilesPanel / EditorPreferencesPanel do this).

## Related skills
`funke-add-profiler` (ProfilerPanel + instrumentation), `funke-author-package` (PackageManagerPanel internals), `funke-inspector-ruleset` (Inspector drawing, not panels), `funke-build-and-ship` (Build / Build Profiles panels' semantics), `funke-code-style`, `funke-comment-style`, `funke-build-engine`.

.agents/skills/funke-add-system/SKILL.md:
---
name: funke-add-system
description: Use when adding a native C++ per-scene system to the Funke engine, or deciding where per-frame engine logic should live. Triggers on "add a system", "new SceneSystem", "AddSystem", "AddStandardSceneSystems", "system execution order", "EnableSystem / DisableSystem / GetSystem", "OnPreRender", "FixedUpdate vs Update", "system runs in edit mode", "ISystem" (old name), or work in `Funke-Engine/src/Systems/`, `Scene/SceneSystem.hpp`, `SceneDefinition.hpp` or an app's `ConfigureScenes()`. Covers the `SceneSystem` hooks, registration (standard set vs per-definition), Funke.2D/Funke.3D module gating, real frame order (Update/FixedUpdate/OnPreRender vs 2D and 3D physics, layers, C# systems), editor edit-vs-play behavior, enable/disable, exceptions and tests. For C# game logic (EntityScript / SceneSystem / GlobalSystem) use `funke-game-scripting`; for editor UI use `funke-add-editor-panel`.
---

# Add a Native Scene System

Native systems derive from `Funke::SceneSystem` (`Funke-Engine/src/Scene/SceneSystem.hpp`; the old `ISystem` is gone). Each `Scene` owns its own instances as `std::vector<std::unique_ptr<SceneSystem>>`, created from factories stored on the `SceneDefinition` when the scene is instantiated, so state is per scene instance and is destroyed with it.

## Choose the right home first

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Per-scene engine behavior over components (animation, layout, audio sync) | Native `SceneSystem` (this skill) |
| Gameplay logic for a project | C# `SceneSystem` / `GlobalSystem` / `EntityScript` (`funke-game-scripting`) — no engine rebuild |
| App-wide, not scene-bound (overlays, tooling, frame hooks, input routing) | `Layer` (`Core/Layer.hpp`: `OnAttach/OnUpdate/OnFixedUpdate/OnPreRender/OnPostRender/OnEvent`), pushed in `ConfigureLayers()`. `GizmosDebugSystem` is a Layer on purpose |
| ImGui / editor UI | Editor panel (`funke-add-editor-panel`). There is no `OnGui` hook on systems |
| Physics stepping | 2D: owned by `Application` (`Physics/PhysicsSystem2D`), not a scene system. 3D: `PhysicsSystem3D` (steps in `FixedUpdate`) and `PhysicsInterpolationSystem3D` (`Update`) are standard scene systems (`Physics3D/PhysicsSystem3D.hpp`) |

## 1. Header + source

`Funke-Engine/src/Systems/MySystem.hpp`:
```cpp
#pragma once
#include "Core/Export.hpp"
#include "Scene/SceneSystem.hpp"

namespace Funke {
	struct MyComponent;

	class FUNKE_API MySystem : public SceneSystem {
	public:
		void Update(Scene& scene) override;

		// Pure per-entity step, exposed so tests can drive it without an Application.
		static void Step(MyComponent& component, float dt);
	};
}
```

`Funke-Engine/src/Systems/MySystem.cpp`:
```cpp
#include "pch.hpp"
#include "Systems/MySystem.hpp"

#include "Components/Tags.hpp"
#include "Core/Application.hpp"
#include "Core/Time.hpp"
#include "Profiling/Profiler.hpp"
#include "Scene/Scene.hpp"

namespace Funke {
	void MySystem::Step(MyComponent& component, float dt) { /* ... */ }

	void MySystem::Update(Scene& scene) {
		if (!Application::GetIsPlaying()) return;   // see "Edit mode" below
		FUNKE_PROFILE_SCOPE("MySystem");
		const float dt = Time::GetDeltaTime();
		auto view = scene.GetRegistry().view<MyComponent>(entt::exclude<DisabledTag>);
		for (auto [entity, component] : view.each()) {
			Step(component, dt);
		}
	}
}
```
Example of a per-entity helper exercised by tests: `Systems/LocalizedTextSystem.{hpp,cpp}` (`Apply`) + `Tests/Funke-Engine-Tests/src/GameLocalizationTests.cpp`. Include specific component headers, not the deprecated `Components/Components.hpp`. Respect `DisabledTag` (and `InheritedDisabledTag` is applied alongside it to children) in views.

## 2. Hooks (all optional, all take `Scene&`)

| Hook | When |
|---|---|
| `Awake` | Scene load, after `OnInitialize`/`OnLoad` callbacks and `ScenePreStartEvent`, before `Start`. Only enabled systems; order recorded for teardown |
| `Start` | Right after all `Awake` calls, same load |
| `Update` | Every frame **only while gameplay is active** (`Application::GetIsPlaying()` and not gameplay-paused) |
| `FixedUpdate` | Each fixed step while playing, **before** the 2D physics step (3D physics steps inside this pass, in `PhysicsSystem3D`) |
| `OnPreRender` | Every frame after Update and physics sync, before rendering — **also in edit mode** |
| `OnEnable` / `OnDisable` | Only on enable-state transitions via `EnableSystem<T>/DisableSystem<T>` (not on load) |
| `OnDestroy` | Scene unload/rollback, in reverse awaken order; also for systems added after Awake |

Every hook runs inside a `SceneExecutionScope`, so implicit-scene APIs (`Entity::Create`, `ResolveImplicitScene()`) target this scene, not the active one.

## 3. Register

**Every scene (engine built-in):** add it to `AddStandardSceneSystems` in `Funke-Engine/src/Scene/SceneManager.cpp`, which `SceneManager::RegisterScene` calls for every definition (editor working/asset scenes, runtime build scenes, C#-loaded scenes). Current order ([2D]/[3D] = only while that engine module is active): [2D] `TransformHierarchySystem` / [3D] `Transform3DHierarchySystem`, `PhysicsInterpolationSystem3D` (first; everyone sees fresh world transforms) → `UILayoutSystem` → [2D] `ParticleUpdateSystem` → [3D] `Particle3DUpdateSystem`, `SkinnedMeshAnimationSystem` → `ScriptSystem` → `AnimatorSystem` → [3D] `PhysicsSystem3D` → `AudioUpdateSystem` → `UIFocusSystem` → `UIEventSystem`, `LocalizedTextSystem` (focus must precede event). Gate on `ApplicationConfig` (`EnableRenderer2D`, `EnableScripting`, `EnableAudio`) like the neighbors. A system using Funke.2D/Funke.3D types also needs the module gate: its include and `AddSystem` inside `#if FUNKE_WITH_2D` / `FUNKE_WITH_3D`, plus the `with2D`/`with3D` check (`EngineModules::IsActive`) — otherwise the `--without-2d|3d` runtime variants stop compiling. Placement relative to `ScriptSystem` decides whether scripts see your results this frame.

**One scene (app-specific):** in the app's `ConfigureScenes()` (`Funke-Runtime/src/RuntimeApplication.cpp`, `Funke-Editor/src/EditorApplication.cpp`, `Funke-Launcher/src/LauncherApplication.cpp`, tests):
```cpp
SceneManager::RegisterScene("Main")
	.AddSystem<MySystem>(ctorArgs...)   // args are captured and forwarded to the ctor
	.SetAsStartupScene();
```
`AddSystem` appends after the standard set and ignores (with a warning) a type already registered on that definition. `SceneManager` is a static API; there is no `SceneManager::Get()` for callers.

## Execution order per frame

Fixed steps (accumulator-driven, catch-up capped) run first: `Application::FixedUpdate()` → managed fixed-update coroutine pump → per scene `FixedUpdate` (playing only; includes the `PhysicsSystem3D` step) → `PhysicsSystem2D::FixedUpdate` → C# `GlobalSystem` fixed update → `Layer::OnFixedUpdate`. Then the frame: C# global systems update (playing) → `Application::Update()` → `Layer::OnUpdate` → managed update coroutine pump → per scene `UpdateSystems` (playing; drains delayed destroys first) → `PhysicsSystem2D::Update` (Transform→physics sync, also in edit mode) → per scene `OnPreRender` → `Layer::OnPreRender` → render. The coroutine pumps run only while gameplay is active and may change that state before scene ticking.

- Scenes tick in loaded-list order (`SceneManager::MoveLoadedScene` changes it); systems in registration order; C# scene systems (`ManagedSceneSystem`, from the scene file's `systems`) are appended after native ones.
- Need post-physics results? 2D: read them in `Update`, not `FixedUpdate` (Box2D steps after every scene's FixedUpdate). 3D: systems after `PhysicsSystem3D` (every `AddSystem` one) already see this step in `FixedUpdate`.

## Edit mode vs play mode (editor)

- Scenes are loaded in edit mode, so `Awake`/`Start` run **without** play having started, and run again when Stop rebuilds scenes from the play snapshot. Pressing Play does not reload scenes or re-run Awake/Start for native systems. Initialize per-play state lazily in `Update` (SpriteAnimation's `Started` flag) or check `Application::GetIsPlaying()`.
- `Update`/`FixedUpdate` don't run in edit mode; `OnPreRender` does — keep it cheap and don't mutate authored component data there (it would leak into the saved scene).
- The runtime sets `Application::SetIsPlaying(true)` before scenes load; the editor sets it false.

## Runtime control

```cpp
scene.EnableSystem<MySystem>();      // calls OnEnable on transition
scene.DisableSystem<MySystem>();     // calls OnDisable on transition
scene.IsSystemEnabled<MySystem>();
scene.HasSystem<MySystem>();
MySystem* sys = scene.GetSystem<MySystem>();   // pointer; nullptr (trace log) if absent
```
Disabled systems skip `Awake`, `Start`, and frame hooks. `OnDisable` runs on the transition, and an already-awakened system still receives `OnDestroy` during teardown even if it was later disabled. Reload creates new system instances with their initial enabled state. Lookups use `dynamic_cast` over the list — cache the pointer if called per entity.

## Exceptions

`Scene::ForeachEnabledSystem` logs `"<type> failed in '<phase>'"` and **rethrows**; nothing swallows per system. Exceptions in Awake/Start fail the load (`SceneLoadStatus::AwakeFailed/StartFailed`) and roll the scene back (`OnDestroy` for already-awakened systems). Throw only for genuine faults; log and skip bad entities.

## Tests (`Tests/Funke-Engine-Tests/src`, doctest)

- Logic: unit-test the static per-entity helper (pattern: `GameLocalizationTests.cpp` exercises `LocalizedTextSystem::Apply`).
- Lifecycle/registration: headless `Application` subclass with `ConfigureScenes()` + assertions in `Start()` then `Application::Quit()` (patterns: `SceneExecutionContextTests.cpp`, `SceneManagerFailureTests.cpp` with `ApplicationConfig::Headless()`). Note `Update` won't run if you quit in `Start`.
- If public API, a `static_assert` in `UmbrellaHeaderTests.cpp` and the include in `Funke-Engine/src/Funke.hpp`.

## Build

Project files list sources explicitly; `scripts\dev\Build.ps1` regenerates premake automatically when it finds a new `.cpp`. File gating: systems needing the renderer belong in `Funke-Engine/premake5.lua`'s `RemoveFilesIfModuleDisabled(FunkeModules.Render, ...)` list (like `UI*System`); Funke.2D/Funke.3D systems in that module's `sources` in `Funke-Engine/EngineModules.json` (like `ParticleUpdateSystem`, `Particle3DUpdateSystem`). Build and deploy per `funke-build-engine`.

